From 03bbbaa2e393739465a5065add8151b028f8c760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 041/108] gpu: vulkan: keep the pipeline storage on Android and
 persist a driver pipeline cache

On Bionic, fopen("a+") leaves the read position at the end of the file, so
the header reads in InitializeShaderStorage always failed and both the .xpso
pipeline storage and the .xsh shader storage were truncated at every start:
no pipeline was ever prewarmed and every run recompiled them during play.
Rewind both streams after opening them.

- StorageWriteThread flushed a batch only after the next request arrived, so
  the last batch stayed in the stdio buffers and was lost on force-stop. Flush
  as soon as the queue drains, and fsync (_commit on Windows).
- Truncate the pipeline storage to the descriptions validated in the file,
  not to those kept for this device (skipped unsupported ones cut valid ones).
- Log the shader and pipeline description counts loaded from the storage.
- Add a driver-level VkPipelineCache owned by the VulkanDevice and pass it to
  every vkCreateGraphicsPipelines/vkCreateComputePipelines call (guest
  pipelines, render target, texture, swap, presenter and immediate drawer
  pipelines). VulkanPipelineCache merges <title>.vk.pipelinecache from the
  shareable storage folder into it before creating the stored pipelines
  (VkPipelineCacheHeaderVersionOne vendor, device and pipelineCacheUUID
  validated, discarded on mismatch) and the storage writer thread saves it
  3 s after the last pipeline creation (at most every 30 s while creations
  continue) and at shutdown, through a temporary file and a rename, skipping
  the write when its size did not change.

Driver cache persistence modelled on leftisthominid/lr-ffxiii-port (GPL-3.0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/vulkan/pipeline_cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/vulkan/pipeline_cache.h
index 7b938b9..43f0eb9 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/vulkan/pipeline_cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/vulkan/pipeline_cache.h
@@ -444,6 +444,27 @@ class VulkanPipelineCache {
   FILE* pipeline_storage_file_ = nullptr;
   bool pipeline_storage_file_flush_needed_ = false;
 
+  // Persistence of the driver-level VkPipelineCache owned by the VulkanDevice (which every
+  // pipeline creation in the Vulkan backend uses), in the shareable storage folder. The file is
+  // merged into the device's cache when the storage is initialized, before the stored pipelines
+  // are created, and is saved by the storage writer thread once new pipeline creations have
+  // settled (the Android app is ended with a force-stop, never a clean shutdown), through a
+  // temporary file and a rename so a kill cannot leave a torn file.
+  static constexpr uint64_t kDriverPipelineCacheSaveSettleMs = 3000;
+  static constexpr uint64_t kDriverPipelineCacheSaveMaxDelayMs = 30000;
+  void LoadDriverPipelineCache(const std::filesystem::path& path);
+  void SaveDriverPipelineCache();
+  // Milliseconds until the driver pipeline cache should be saved, or -1 if nothing new to save.
+  int64_t GetDriverPipelineCacheSaveDelayMs() const;
+  void MarkDriverPipelineCacheUsed();
+  std::filesystem::path driver_pipeline_cache_path_;
+  std::mutex driver_pipeline_cache_save_mutex_;
+  // Size of the data last loaded or saved, to skip saves when nothing new was compiled.
+  size_t driver_pipeline_cache_saved_size_ = 0;
+  std::atomic<uint64_t> driver_pipeline_cache_last_use_ms_{0};
+  // 0 when there are no pipeline creations since the last save.
+  std::atomic<uint64_t> driver_pipeline_cache_first_unsaved_use_ms_{0};
+
   // Thread for asynchronous writing to the storage streams.
   void StorageWriteThread();
   std::mutex storage_write_request_lock_;
